   "created_by_ref": "identity--df314057-d669-5e4d-aa9c-5257582a7ecd",
   "description": "MidnightFrost detection notes\n\nThe following YARA rule detects the MidnightFrost loader in memory:\n\nrule MidnightFrost_Loader {\n    meta:\n        description = \"MidnightFrost loader strings\"\n    strings:\n        $a = \"FrostSvc\" ascii\n        $b = \"MidnightFrostMtx\" wide\n    condition:\n        any of them\n}\n\nA second rule is broken in the report (its condition names a string that does not exist):\n\nrule Broken_Rule {\n    strings:\n        $a = \"oops\"\n    condition:\n        $nonexistent\n}\n\nThe network side is covered by this Suricata rule:\n\nalert http $HOME_NET any -> $EXTERNAL_NET any (msg:\"MidnightFrost beacon\"; content:\"/stage/payload.bin\"; http.uri; sid:1000001; rev:1;)\n\nSnort users can use the older rule below.\nalert tcp $HOME_NET any -> $EXTERNAL_NET 4444 (msg:\"MidnightFrost reverse shell\"; flow:to_server,established; content:\"|de ad be ef|\"; sid:1000002; rev:1;)\n\nThe host indicators are 91.215.85.17, frostmail-cdn.test and the hash e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855.\n\nSigma rule for the registry persistence:\n\ntitle: MidnightFrost Run Key Persistence\nid: 5f1c1d52-3c2b-4a58-9d1f-0b8f9a3c7e11\nstatus: experimental\ndescription: Detects the FrostSvc Run key written by MidnightFrost\nlogsource:\n    category: registry_set\n    product: windows\ndetection:\n    selection:\n        TargetObject|endswith: '\\CurrentVersion\\Run\\FrostSvc'\n    condition: selection\nlevel: high",
   "external_references": [
    {
     "description": "Original CTI report: midnightfrost_rules.md",
     "source_name": "original_document"
    }
   ],
